High-dispersion spectra were also taken on two nights (2014 February 05, phase 0.861, and April 10, phase 0.064) using the Canada France Hawaii Telescope/ESPaDOnS (Manset & Donati, 2003) in spectropolarimetric mode. The spectra covered a wavelength range of 3700-10 500 A with a resolving power of \\sim 68\\,000. We obtained reduced data using the Libre-Esprit/Upena2 pipeline, provided by the instrument team. We rectified the normalized intensity by re-determining the continuum level around each line, in order to compare with HIDES data. In this paper, we focus on the spectroscopic variability. The polarimetric data will be discussed in a forthcoming paper.

